	<string></string>
	<key>MeloCrashReportingDSN</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>MeloDiagnosticsEndpoint</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<!-- Rewritten for 3.1: Melo Edit can record system audio, so the old
	     promise that Melo never records was no longer true. Recording needs no
	     new permission — it is the same Screen & System Audio Recording grant
	     the live path already asks for — so this is a truer sentence rather
	     than a bigger ask. It does not name Melo Edit: this prompt
	     appears at first launch, before anyone knows what that is, and the
	     record sheet does that work at the moment it means something. -->
	<string>Melo adjusts the volume and tone of each app you control and plays that audio straight back. It records only when you start a recording, and that file stays on this Mac.</string>
